# tally 2.2.1 S-232 (L §5.19 "each observation that stands (§4.6)"; E §3.1 step 9: LOAD-COVERS "on the rows that
# stand, per world and cut class"; P19):
# scenario narrowed moves register_10 to 2026-10-01..2026-10-20; r2 on 10-28 stands in its world:
# the scenario is refused. tally 2.2's refcore loaded it (T's held fixture/reviews/narrowed).
=== options check exit=1
=== m.tally
model narrow
  tally 2
  on 2026-11-05
  start 2026-10-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T's base for #232's second case (invented): a register covering konto in October with two bank rows, one on 10-10 and one on 10-28"

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01


place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input bank: observed

version home
  cite s
  governs 2026-10..
  known 2026-10-01
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-10-01 start "wyciąg"

version register_10
  cite s
  governs 2026-10
  known 2026-11-02
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-10-10, kind: transfers, leg cash from world to konto amount 500.00 PLN) "line 1"
  bank[r2] = (on: 2026-10-28, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 120.00 PLN) "line 2"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-10-31)
=== s.tally
scenario narrowed over narrow
  tally 2
  from 2026-10-01

version narrowed_coverage
  cite s
  governs 2026-10..
  known 2026-11-03
  moves register_10 to 2026-10-01..2026-10-20

ask q_narrowed: bal(konto, 2026-10-31) in narrowed
=== expect
scenario narrowed: refused: LOAD-COVERS observation bank[r2] of konto is dated outside the span register_10 covers (m.tally:30)
